 I exercised my  whole life after medical tests Dawn had  an embryo made with a donor egg and  donor sperm implanted I said to Mike I  said I just don't believe there it's  gonna work anyway so on the 23rd of  December when we got on the 23 December  wait wait wait I went over to the  drugstore and got the cut the actual  pregnancy test yeah I'm the technical  guy so I did the different and basically  I can balance is by the way you're 2 to  3 weeks pregnant yeah and at that point  we're just like okay because you don't  know after you're going I was shocked  and I was shocked totally shocked you  know this is a miracle  the total number of fertility clinics  around the world is estimated to have  increased by almost 70 percent in the  last 10 years  [Music]  the value of the global fertility  industry is predicted to rise from 25  billion dollars today to 41 billion  dollars by 2026  [Music]  many believe there needs to be more  regulation of an increasingly globalised  IVF trade including dr. Daniel Lane a  fertility specialist based in San  Francisco I think that the risks far  outweigh the benefits of being pregnant  at 65  we do not do embryo transfers and anyone  who's above the age of 50 however dr.  Lane is using new technology that will  allow more women to have children later  in life we are definitely seeing an  increase in egg freezing so clearly the  trend is that women are delaying their  childbearing in 2017 the number of women  freezing their own eggs in America  jumped by nearly a quarter in one year  alone  dr. Lane believes this will help some  women balance their careers and families  more effectively in the future now we're  saying you can have that child at 40  using your 28 year old eggs so maybe it  matters that you spend those extra 10  years focused on your career and get to  a point where you feel comfortable  having that baby at 40  there is another technological  development that might accelerate this  trend towards older parents  today 